# The behavioural identity each arbiter must report, exactly as the verdict
# corpus records it. A verdict is keyed on this string, so a container that
# reports anything else forks the corpus rather than adding to it.
#
# Captured from the corpus, not typed from memory:
#   jq -r '.arbiter | "\(.tool)\t\(.identity)"' verdicts/*.ndjson | sort -u
#
# `vasmm68k_mot` reads 2.0f, not the 2.0b the corpus was first built on:
# upstream keeps no versioned archives and has moved on, so the version was
# adopted deliberately rather than pinned to something nobody can fetch. The
# 436 verdicts recorded under 2.0b are superseded and re-arbitrated separately.
#
